1	/**
2	 * Postgres-backed Chat SDK `StateAdapter` implemented against the shared
3	 * `getDb()` postgres-js client.
4	 *
5	 * Why we own this instead of using `@chat-adapter/state-pg`:
6	 *   - state-pg requires a `pg.Pool` (node-postgres). Lobu otherwise speaks
7	 *     postgres-js everywhere, so depending on state-pg meant carrying both
8	 *     drivers + a second connection pool just to keep one upstream library
9	 *     happy.
10	 *   - The schema is small (5 tables) and the methods are plain CRUD with
11	 *     TTL filtering. Nothing here is upstream IP — keeping it in-tree is
12	 *     cheaper than the dep weight.
13	 *
14	 * Schema lives in `db/migrations/00000000000000_baseline.sql` (the post-2026-05-19
15	 * squashed baseline that absorbed the original 20260519020000_chat_state_tables
16	 * migration). All boot paths — production runner, embedded start-local — apply the
17	 * baseline; no separate mirror to maintain. Table names and column types match
18	 * `@chat-adapter/state-pg`'s so an existing state-pg deployment can swap in
19	 * this adapter without a schema migration.
20	 *
21	 * Concurrency: every method works on a single statement that round-trips
22	 * through the pool; no in-class state. Multiple gateways on the same DB
23	 * coordinate via row-level locks (acquire/release) and `ON CONFLICT`.
24	 */
